# Stack

## Languages
- Backend:  Rust (stable, pinned in `rust-toolchain.toml`) — Cargo workspace
- Frontend: Askama + HTMX, served by the backend. No Node build step.

## Commands

### Build
- Debug:    `cargo build --workspace --all-targets`
- Release:  `cargo build --release --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl`

### Test
- All:      `cargo test --workspace`
- Property: `cargo test --workspace -- --include-ignored`

### Type Check / Lint
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`

### Format
- Apply: `cargo fmt --all`
- Check: `cargo fmt --all -- --check`

## Quality Tools (install if missing)

Each analyzer below MUST conform to the Analyzer Contract: accepts a path,
emits a single JSON document to stdout (`tool`, `metric`, `threshold`,
`violations`, optional `summary`), exits 0 on pass and non-zero on any
violation.

No Rust tool emits the contract natively. Each `Run` is a wrapper under
`scripts/analyzers/` that reshapes the underlying tool's output.

- Coverage:    cargo-llvm-cov
  Install:     `rustup component add llvm-tools-preview && cargo install cargo-llvm-cov`
  Run:         `scripts/analyzers/coverage.sh <path>`
  Threshold:   80  # minimum coverage (%)

- Mutation:    cargo-mutants
  Install:     `cargo install cargo-mutants`
  Run:         `scripts/analyzers/mutation.sh <path>`
  Threshold:   90  # minimum kill rate (%)
  Parallelism: scheduler-core: 8   |   every other crate: 1
  # scheduler-core is pure, so its mutants are safely parallel. Other crates
  # share one SQLite file; parallel mutants truncate each other's database and
  # the symptom is timeouts, not an obvious collision. Do not raise the timeout.

- Complexity:  rust-code-analysis-cli
  Install:     `cargo install rust-code-analysis-cli`
  Run:         `scripts/analyzers/complexity.sh <path>`
  Threshold:   8   # max cyclomatic complexity per function
  # Derived, not conventional: the largest enum in the domain model has 5
  # variants, so an exhaustive `match` over it scores 6. 8 leaves headroom for
  # one guard on top of that and still flags real branching. A function over 8
  # is carrying logic that is not the match -- extract that, do not flatten the
  # match into if/else.

- CRAP:        custom — composes the coverage and complexity analyzers
  Install:     none
  Run:         `scripts/analyzers/crap.sh <path>`
  Threshold:   30  # exclusive upper bound per function

- DRY:         jscpd
  Install:     `npm i -g jscpd`
  Run:         `scripts/analyzers/dry.sh <path>`
  Threshold:   3   # max % duplicated tokens

- Lint:        clippy
  Install:     `rustup component add clippy`
  Run:         `scripts/analyzers/lint.sh <path>`
  Threshold:   0   # zero warnings, zero errors

## Additional Verification
- Tests:       all pass
- Format:      `cargo fmt --all -- --check` is clean
- Core purity: `cargo tree -p scheduler-core` contains no `tokio` and no `sqlx`
